.TH fleetring-cert 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-cert \- Creates the authority, and issues node and client certificates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring cert\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates the authority, and issues node and client certificates
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fleetring\-cert\-init(1)
Creates the authority: `ca.crt` and `ca.key` in the directory
.TP
fleetring\-cert\-node(1)
Issues a node certificate: `node.<id>.crt` and `node.<id>.key`
.TP
fleetring\-cert\-client(1)
Issues a client certificate, naming the principal the client acts as
.TP
fleetring\-cert\-issuer(1)
Issues a delegation issuer pair: `issuer.<name>.crt` and `issuer.<name>.key`
